+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+Defect pinned this leg (external browser acceptance suite, fixed and correct):
+
+- Failures 1-4 (Mark all completed; Item mark/unmark): `render()` in `js/app.js`
+  does `list.innerHTML = ''` and rebuilds every `<li>`. A browser reference taken
+  before a click (toggle one, `#toggle-all` check/uncheck) is detached when the
+  list rebuilds, so a chain off that held element fails with "element has
+  detached from the DOM". Fix: mutate the existing nodes in place (toggle the
+  `completed` class / checkbox, update counts and the `#toggle-all` state) rather
+  than rebuilding the list. Node identity must survive toggles, mark-all, and
+  clear-completed (the surviving active nodes must stay attached; only genuinely
+  removed todos may detach).
+
+- Failure 5 (Editing hides other controls): the served page ships no stylesheet.
+  `index.html` links `css/app.css` and `node_modules/todomvc-app-css/index.css`,
+  but neither exists in the tree, so `.view` (toggle + label) is never hidden
+  while a todo is edited. Fix: ship `css/app.css` with the rule that hides the
+  todo view controls when a `li` carries the `editing` class. This is a
+  browser-only behaviour; the in-harness guard asserts the served page links and
+  ships that stylesheet.
+
+Pinned by: `features/dom-identity.feature` (failures 1-4) and
+`features/index-page.feature` (failure 5, served-page guard). Targeted by
+`watchbill.json` (watch1, watch2).
+
+Next leg: QM authors the missing step definitions (capture a DOM node; assert it
+is still attached; served-page stylesheet link/hide checks). Crew fixes the
+re-render and ships the stylesheet. The acceptance suite is fixed and correct;
+do not change it.
