@@ -0,0 +1,61 @@
+Feature: DOM node identity
+  When the app changes a todo's state it must mutate the existing DOM nodes in
+  place instead of rebuilding the whole list, so a node reference a browser
+  holds across the interaction stays attached to the document. The current
+  render rebuilds every <li> (list.innerHTML = ''), which detaches nodes a
+  browser captured before the click and breaks acceptance flows that chain off
+  a held element. These scenarios hold a direct node reference, perform the
+  state change, then assert the held node is still attached.
+
+  Rule: Toggling one todo preserves the other todo elements in the list
+
+  Scenario: Toggling one todo keeps the other todos' DOM nodes attached
+    Given the app loads with todos:
+      | title            | completed |
+      | Buy a unicorn    | false     |
+      | Taste JavaScript | false     |
+      | Rule the web     | false     |
+    And I capture the DOM node for the "Taste JavaScript" todo
+    When the "Buy a unicorn" todo checkbox is clicked
+    Then the captured todo node is still attached to the document
+
+  Scenario: Toggling one todo keeps that todo's own DOM node attached and marks it complete
+    Given the app loads with todos:
+      | title            | completed |
+      | Buy a unicorn    | false     |
+      | Taste JavaScript | false     |
+    And I capture the DOM node for the "Buy a unicorn" todo
+    When the "Buy a unicorn" todo checkbox is clicked
+    Then the captured todo node is still attached to the document
+    And the captured todo node has class "completed"
+
+  Rule: Marking all or clearing all preserves every todo element
+
+  Scenario: Marking all complete keeps every todo's DOM node attached
+    Given the app loads with todos:
+      | title            | completed |
+      | Buy a unicorn    | false     |
+      | Taste JavaScript | false     |
+    And I capture the DOM node for the "Taste JavaScript" todo
+    When "#toggle-all" is clicked
+    Then the captured todo node is still attached to the document
+
+  Scenario: Clearing the complete state of all items keeps every todo's DOM node attached
+    Given the app loads with todos:
+      | title            | completed |
+      | Buy a unicorn    | false     |
+      | Taste JavaScript | false     |
+    And I capture the DOM node for the "Taste JavaScript" todo
+    When "#toggle-all" is clicked
+    And "#toggle-all" is clicked
+    Then the captured todo node is still attached to the document
+
+  Scenario: Clearing completed keeps the surviving todos' DOM nodes attached
+    Given the app loads with todos:
+      | title            | completed |
+      | Buy a unicorn    | false     |
+      | Taste JavaScript | true      |
+    And I capture the DOM node for the "Buy a unicorn" todo
+    When the ".clear-completed" button is clicked
+    Then the captured todo node is still attached to the document
+    And only the "Buy a unicorn" todo remains
